मणोरणीयांसमनुस्मरेद्य: ।
सर्वस्य धातारमचिन्त्यरूप-
मादित्यवर्णं तमस: परस्तात् ॥ ९ ॥\"}]},{\"section\":\"verse_text\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.verse-text\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"verse_text\",\"id\":2409,\"bb\":2136,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/8/9/b2136/\",\"body_value\":\"kaviṁ purāṇam anuśāsitāram
aṇor aṇīyāṁsam anusmared yaḥ
sarvasya dhātāram acintya-rūpam
āditya-varṇaṁ tamasaḥ parastāt\"}]},{\"section\":\"synonyms\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.synonyms\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"books.Synonyms\",\"title\":\"synonyms\",\"id\":2410,\"bb\":2137,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/8/9/b2137/\",\"shadow_value\":\"kavim – the one who knows everything; purāṇam – the oldest; anuśāsitāram – the controller; aṇoḥ – than the atom; aṇīyāṁsam – smaller; anusmaret – always thinks of; yaḥ – one who; sarvasya – of everything; dhātāram – the maintainer; acintya – inconceivable; rūpam – whose form; āditya-varṇam – luminous like the sun; tamasaḥ – to darkness; parastāt – transcendental.\",\"word_for_word_value\":[{\"word\":\"kavim\",\"translation\":\"the one who knows everything\"},{\"word\":\"purāṇam\",\"translation\":\"the oldest\"},{\"word\":\"anuśāsitāram\",\"translation\":\"the controller\"},{\"word\":\"aṇoḥ\",\"translation\":\"than the atom\"},{\"word\":\"aṇīyāṁsam\",\"translation\":\"smaller\"},{\"word\":\"anusmaret\",\"translation\":\"always thinks of\"},{\"word\":\"yaḥ\",\"translation\":\"one who\"},{\"word\":\"sarvasya\",\"translation\":\"of everything\"},{\"word\":\"dhātāram\",\"translation\":\"the maintainer\"},{\"word\":\"acintya\",\"translation\":\"inconceivable\"},{\"word\":\"rūpam\",\"translation\":\"whose form\"},{\"word\":\"āditya-varṇam\",\"translation\":\"luminous like the sun\"},{\"word\":\"tamasaḥ\",\"translation\":\"to darkness\"},{\"word\":\"parastāt\",\"translation\":\"transcendental\"}]}]},{\"section\":\"translation\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.translation\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"translation\",\"id\":2411,\"bb\":2138,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/8/9/b2138/\",\"body_value\":\"One should meditate upon the Supreme Person as the one who knows everything, as He who is the oldest, who is the controller, who is smaller than the smallest, who is the maintainer of everything, who is beyond all material conception, who is inconceivable, and who is always a person. He is luminous like