:\"bhaktyā\"}]}]],\" — \",[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"inline\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"in full devotion\"}}],\"; \"]}],[\"$\",\"span\",\"wfwundefined-4\",{\"className\":\"inline\",\"children\":[[[\"$\",\"$L20\",\"wfwundefined-0-yuktaḥ\",{\"href\":\"/en/search/synonyms/?original=yuktaḥ\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"em\",null,{\"children\":\"yuktaḥ\"}]}]],\" — \",[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"inline\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"engaged\"}}],\"; \"]}],[\"$\",\"span\",\"wfwundefined-5\",{\"className\":\"inline\",\"children\":[[[\"$\",\"$L20\",\"wfwundefined-0-yoga\",{\"href\":\"/en/search/synonyms/?original=yoga\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"em\",null,{\"children\":\"yoga\"}]}],\"-\",[\"$\",\"$L20\",\"wfwundefined-2-balena\",{\"href\":\"/en/search/synonyms/?original=balena\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"em\",null,{\"children\":\"balena\"}]}]],\" — \",[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"inline\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"by the power of mystic yoga\"}}],\"; \"]}],[\"$\",\"span\",\"wfwundefined-6\",{\"className\":\"inline\",\"children\":[[[\"$\",\"$L20\",\"wfwundefined-0-ca\",{\"href\":\"/en/search/synonyms/?original=ca\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"em\",null,{\"children\":\"ca\"}]}]],\" — \",[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"inline\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"also\"}}],\"; \"]}],[\"$\",\"span\",\"wfwundefined-7\",{\"className\":\"inline\",\"children\":[[[\"$\",\"$L20\",\"wfwundefined-0-eva\",{\"href\":\"/en/search/synonyms/?original=eva\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"em\",null,{\"children\":\"eva\"}]}]],\" — \",[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"inline\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"certainly\"}}],\"; \"]}],[\"$\",\"span\",\"wfwundefined-8\",{\"className\":\"inline\",\"children\":[[[\"$\",\"$L20\",\"wfwundefined-0-bhruvoḥ\",{\"href\":\"/en/search/synonyms/?original=bhruvoḥ\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"em\",null,{\"children\":\"bhruvoḥ\"}]}]],\" — \",[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"inline\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"the two eyebrows\"}}],\"; \"]}],[\"$\",\"span\",\"wfwundefined-9\",{\"className\":\"inline\",\"children\":[[[\"$\",\"$L20\",\"wfwundefined-0-madhye\",{\"href\":\"/en/search/synonyms/?original=madhye\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"em\",null,{\"children\":\"madhye\"}]}]],\" — \",[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"inline\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"between\"}}],\"; \"]}],[\"$\",\"span\",\"wfwundefined-10\",{\"className\":\"inline\",\"children\":[[[\"$\",\"$L20\",\"wfwundefined-0-prāṇam\",{\"href\":\"/en/search/synonyms/?original=prāṇam\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"em\",null,{\"children\":\"prāṇam\"}]}]],\" — \",[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"inline\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"the life air\"}}],\"; \"]}],[\"$\",\"span\",\"wfwundefined-11\",{\"className\":\"inline\",\"children\":[[[\"$\",\"$L20\",\"wfwundefined-0-āveśya\",{\"href\":\"/en/search/synonyms/?original=āveśya\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"em\",null,{\"children\":\"āveśya\"}]}]],\" — \",[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"inline\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"establishing\"}}],\"; \"]}],[\"$\",\"span\",\"wfwundefined-12\",{\"className\":\"inline\",\"children\":[[[\"$\",\"$L20\",\"wfwundefined-0-samyak\",{\"href\":\"/en/search/synonyms/?original=samyak\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"em\",null,{\"children\":\"samyak\"}]}]],\" — \",[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"inline\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"completely\"}}],\"; \"]}],\"$L31\",\"$L32\",\"$L33\",\"$L34\",\"$L35\",\"$L36\"]}]}]]]}]\n"])self.__next_f.push([1,"2d:[\"$\",\"div\",\"2413-translation,2413-translation\",{\"className\":\"av-translation\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-center em-leading-5 em-text-xl font-bold em-mb-4\",\"children\":\"Translation\"}],[[\"$\",\"$L29\",\"child-2417\",{\"child\":\"$23:props:children:0:props:children:props:page:child_items:3:children:0\",\"hasId\":true,\"children\":[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"em-mb-4 em-leading-8 em-text-base s-justify\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"One who, at the time of death, fixes his life air between the eyebrows and, by the strength of yoga, with an undeviating mind, engages himself in remembering the Supreme Lord in full devotion, will certainly attain to the Supreme Personality of Godhead.\"}}]}]}]]]}]\n"])self.__next_f.push([1,"2e:[\"$\",\"div\",\"2413-purport,2413-purport\",{\"className\":\"av-purport\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-center em-leading-5 em-text-xl font-bold em-mb-4\",\"children\":\"Purport\"}],[[\"$\",\"$L29\",\"child-2418\",{\"child\":\"$23:props:children:0:props:children:props:page:child_items:4:children:0\",\"hasId\":true,\"children\":[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"em-mb-4 em-leading-8 em-text-base s-justify\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"In this verse it is clearly stated that at the time of death the mind must be fixed in devotion to the Supreme Personality of Godhead. For those practiced in yoga, it is recommended that they raise the life force between the eyebrows (to the ājñā-cakra). The practice of ṣaṭ-cakra-yoga, involving meditation on the six cakras, is suggested here. A pure devotee does not practice such yoga, but because he is always engaged in Kṛṣṇa consciousness, at death he can remember the Supreme Personality of Godhead by His grace. This is explained in verse 14.\"}}]}],[\"$\",\"$L29\",\"child-2419\",{\"child\":\"$23:props:children:0:props:children:props:page:child_items:4:children:1\",\"hasId\":true,\"children\":[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"em-mb-4 em-leading-8 em-text-base s-justify\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"The particular use of the word yoga-balena is significant in this verse because without practice of yoga – whether ṣaṭ-cakra-yoga or bhakti-yoga – one cannot come to this transcendental state of being at the time of death. One cannot suddenly remember the Supreme Lord at death; one must have practiced some yoga system, especially the system of bhakti-yoga. Since one’s mind at death is very disturbed, one should practice transcendence through yoga during one’s life.\"}}]}]]]}]\n"])self.__next_f.push([1,"37:[[\"$\",\"source\",null,{\"srcSet\":\"https://simpleanalyticsbadges.com/vedabase.io?mode=auto\",\"media\":\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"}],[\"$\",\"img\",null,{\"src\":\"https://simpleanalyticsbadges.com/vedabase.io?mode=auto\",\"loading\":\"lazy\",\"referrerPolicy\":\"no-referrer\",\"crossOrigin\":\"anonymous\"}]]\n"])self.__next_f.push([1,"26:[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"id\":\"footer\",\"className\":\"mt-auto w-full max-w-7xl mx-auto pt-3 mb-6 text-sm text-vb-normal-text/80 text-center\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L1f\",null,{\"donors\":\"Shweta Saxena; Gopalakrishnan Soundarajan;    Kuldip Persaud;  Raghava Chandra Dasa; Shubhangi Rajiv Panjiyar; Suparna Kotaru;  Rajendra and Geeta Ramchandani;  Jaykumar Prabhakar; Bharat Vyas; Shri Chander Mohan Gilhotra, HG Prashant Mukund Das, Shri Trilok Singh Grover, HG Bhakta Mitra Das, Laxmi Narayan Agarwal; Ronak Talati; Bhargav Ashok; Akiralali; Rajasa das; Riya and Tejal Chopade; Indradyumna Swami; Jai Devaki Parks;  Ashmi Chakraborty; Hari-kirtana das; Ramesta das; Prasad Buddhavarapu; Kresna Sucandra; Esekiel Jaggernauth\",\"locale\":\"en\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"w-full max-w-screen-xl mx-auto text-vb-normal-text mb-3\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"target\":\"_blank\",\"rel\":\"noopener noreferrer\",\"href\":\"https://t.me/online_vedabase\",\"className\":\"text-vb-normal-text hover:text-vb-normal-text/60\",\"alt\":\"Vedabase Telegram\",\"aria-label\":\"Vedabase Telegram\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"svg\",null,{\"stroke\":\"currentColor\",\"fill\":\"currentColor\",\"strokeWidth\":\"0\",\"viewBox\":\"0 0 496 512\",\"className\":\"inline w-8 h-8 mr-4\",\"children\":[\"$undefined\",[[\"$\",\"path\",\"0\",{\"d\":\"M248 8C111 8 0 119 0 256s111 248 248 248 248-111 248-248S385 8 248 8zm121