10/\",\"title\":\"TEXT 10\",\"has_advanced_view\":false,\"translations\":[\"en\",\"cs\",\"es\",\"bg\",\"pt-br\",\"ru\",\"sk\",\"hr\",\"pl\",\"da\",\"de\",\"et\",\"fr\",\"hu\",\"ko\",\"lt\",\"nl\",\"sl\",\"uk\",\"ja\"]},\"next\":{\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/8/12/\",\"title\":\"TEXT 12\",\"has_advanced_view\":false,\"translations\":[\"en\",\"cs\",\"es\",\"bg\",\"pt-br\",\"ru\",\"sk\",\"hr\",\"pl\",\"da\",\"de\",\"et\",\"fr\",\"hu\",\"ko\",\"lt\",\"nl\",\"sl\",\"uk\",\"ja\"]}},\"child_items\":[{\"section\":\"devanagari\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.devanagari\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"content.DevanagariRecord\",\"title\":\"devanagari\",\"id\":2421,\"bb\":568190,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/8/11/devanagari/\",\"body_final\":\"यदक्षरं वेदविदो वदन्ति
विशन्ति यद्यतयो वीतरागा: ।
यदिच्छन्तो ब्रह्मचर्यं चरन्ति
तत्ते पदं सङ्ग्रहेण प्रवक्ष्ये ॥ ११ ॥\"}]},{\"section\":\"verse_text\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.verse-text\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"verse_text\",\"id\":2422,\"bb\":2147,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/8/11/b2147/\",\"body_value\":\"yad akṣaraṁ veda-vido vadanti
viśanti yad yatayo vīta-rāgāḥ
yad icchanto brahma-caryaṁ caranti
tat te padaṁ saṅgraheṇa pravakṣye\"}]},{\"section\":\"synonyms\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.synonyms\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"books.Synonyms\",\"title\":\"synonyms\",\"id\":2423,\"bb\":2148,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/8/11/b2148/\",\"shadow_value\":\"yat – that which; akṣaram – syllable oṁ; veda-vidaḥ – persons conversant with the Vedas; vadanti – say; viśanti – enter; yat – in which; yatayaḥ – great sages; vīta-rāgāḥ – in the renounced order of life; yat – that which; icchantaḥ – desiring; brahma-caryam – celibacy; caranti – practice; tat – that; te – unto you; padam – situation; saṅgraheṇa – in summary; pravakṣye – I shall explain.\",\"word_for_word_value\":[{\"word\":\"yat\",\"translation\":\"that which\"},{\"word\":\"akṣaram\",\"translation\":\"syllable oṁ\"},{\"word\":\"veda-vidaḥ\",\"translation\":\"persons conversant with the Vedas\"},{\"word\":\"vadanti\",\"translation\":\"say\"},{\"word\":\"viśanti\",\"translation\":\"enter\"},{\"word\":\"yat\",\"translation\":\"in which\"},{\"word\":\"yatayaḥ\",\"translation\":\"great sages\"},{\"word\":\"vīta-rāgāḥ\",\"translation\":\"in the renounced order of life\"},{\"word\":\"yat\",\"translation\":\"that which\"},{\"word\":\"icchantaḥ\",\"translation\":\"desiring\"},{\"word\":\"brahma-caryam\",\"translation\":\"celibacy\"},{\"word\":\"caranti\",\"translation\":\"practice\"},{\"word\":\"tat\",\"translation\":\"that\"},{\"word\":\"te\",\"translation\":\"unto you\"},{\"word\":\"padam\",\"translation\":\"situation\"},{\"word\":\"saṅgraheṇa\",\"translation\":\"in summary\"},{\"word\":\"pravakṣye\",\"translation\":\"I shall explain\"}]}]},{\"section\":\"translation\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.translation\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"translation\",\"id\":2424,\"bb\":2149,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/8/11/b2149/\",\"body_value\":\"Persons who are learned in the Vedas, who utter oṁ-kāra, and who are great sages in the renounced order enter into Brahman. Desiring such perfection, one practices celibacy. I shall now briefly explain to you this process by which one may attain salvation.\"}]},{\"section\":\"purport\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.purport\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"paragraph\",\"id\":2425,\"bb\":2150,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/8/11/b2150/\",\"body_value\":\"Lord Śrī Kṛṣṇa has recommended to Arjuna the practice of ṣaṭ-cakra-yoga, in which one places the air of life between the eyebrows. Taking it for granted that Arjuna might not know how to practice ṣaṭ-cakra-yoga, the Lord explains the process in the following verses. The Lord says that Brahman, although one without a second, has various manifestations and features. Especially for the impersonalists, the akṣara, or oṁ-kāra – the syllable oṁ – is identical with Brahman. Kṛṣṇa here explains the impersonal Brahman, into which the renounced order of sages enter.\"},{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"paragraph\",\"id\":2426,\"bb\":2151,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/8/11/b2151/\",\"body_value\":\"$25\"}]}],\"short_title\":\"Bg. 8.11\",\"medium_title\":\"Bhagavad-gītā As It Is 8.11\"},\"locale\":\"en\",\"activeView\":\"$6:props:activeView\"}]}],\"$L26\",\"$L27\",\"$L28\"]}]\n"])self.__next_f.push([1,"2a:I[83068,[\"/_next/static/chunks/130enlymdm.jk.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0b6f_zxj9ay~6.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/143cg6c13uly6.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/07vk.k35-e~ti.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0j6k6n9cniknh.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0.zxv9arc6a56.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/00-zmo-3n1bt8.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0p4z5tusn0jt6.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/01mcazkjru_is.js\"],\"default\"]\n30:I[78455,[\"/_next/static/chunks/130enlymdm.jk.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0b6f_zxj9ay~6.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/143cg6c13uly6.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/07vk.k35-e~ti.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0j6k6n9cniknh.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0.zxv9arc6a56.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/00-zmo-3n1bt8.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0p4z5tusn0jt6.js\",\"/_next